From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 23:50:32 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: NodeIterator and TreeWalker, getElementsByTagNameNS,
 createCDATASection, inputEncoding

document.createNodeIterator and document.createTreeWalker were not there
(libraries that clean or search markup, such as sanitizers, need them in
document mode 9 and later). They now make the iterators of the engine and
wrap them in NodeIterator and TreeWalker objects (root, whatToShow, filter,
nextNode, previousNode, detach; currentNode, parentNode, firstChild,
lastChild, previousSibling, nextSibling). The filter may be a function or an
object with acceptNode; its result 1, 2 or 3 (a true or false result is
accepted too) says accept, reject or skip.

Also document.getElementsByTagNameNS and element.getElementsByTagNameNS,
document.createCDATASection (the engine refuses it in an HTML document) and
document.inputEncoding.

